        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1087,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1072,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1088,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154046,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1088,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154047,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> atypical genital naevus; atypical melanocytic naevus of special site.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154048,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154049,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AMNGT is most commonly located on the labia majora or mons pubis. AMNGT affecting the labia minora is less frequent.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154050,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AMNGT presents as a slow-growing, irregularly pigmented (tan, brown) papule, often &gt;&nbsp;6&nbsp;mm. It is usually an incidental finding. Patients with AMNGT often have a personal or family history of dysplastic naevus {18162770; 21366454} [[Prieto VG, Pfeifer JD, Wick MR. Genital Naevus. In Elder DE, Massi D, Scolyer RA, et al., editors. WHO Classification of Skin Tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2018. (WHO classification of tumours series, 4th ed.; vol. 11). https://publications.iarc.who.int/560.]] [[Moran JMT, Hartsough EM, Hoang MP. Vulvovaginal Melanocytic Lesions: A Review. Diagnostic Histopathology 2024;30:15&ndash;24.]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154051,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AMNGT is mainly found in young women in the third decade of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154052,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154053,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AMNGTs of genital type frequently harbour <em>BRAF </em>NM_004333.4:c.1799T&gt;A p.(Val600Glu) (<em>BRAF </em>V600E) mutations {24842760}; they do not display the anomalies found in mucosal melanomas {27220476}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154054,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a papular lesion, usually pigmented, &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154055,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AMNGT is typically a compound, rather symmetrical melanocytic proliferation with architectural and at least focal cytological atypia of the junctional and (to a lesser degree) dermal components. The junctional nests are usually large, irregularly shaped, and confluent and often show a loss of cohesion among the melanocytes. The melanocytes tend to be larger than in a common naevus and may show mild cytological atypia such as visible nucleoli and abundant heavily pigmented or foamy cytoplasm. Pagetoid growth is usually absent; when present, it is confined to the centre of the lesion. The periphery of the lesion sometimes displays a single-cell lentiginous growth pattern. The dermal/subepithelial component usually consists of dispersed nests, horizontal rows, or sheets of smaller melanocytes. There may be prominent stromal fibroplasia. Cytological atypia is less prominent in the subepithelial/dermal component than in the junctional component. Mitotic activity is low but can be found superficially.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154056,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154057,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154058,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> at least focally prominent architectural atypia in the junctional component; mostly symmetrical lesion with maturation with depth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154059,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154060,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AMNGT behaves in a benign fashion without recurrence when completely removed.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]